                        "entry_id": "c031d880-a140-3cc5-9853-4b012d9107bd",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A small concavity or depression between ridges, where rainwater gathers."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Australia"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "35400634-01f7-4958-b5ab-fdb6e4c32585",
                                "sense_id": "de4ad0e1-34de-3a25-9f1f-0a74bde425a4",
                                "text": "Though it wasn′t a heavy storm it was enough to put water in gilgai holes and scatter the horses."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "916ad06b-ca75-4629-92e8-05ea6ddd731e",
                                "sense_id": "de4ad0e1-34de-3a25-9f1f-0a74bde425a4",
                                "text": "Argilliturbation is manifested within Vertisol profiles and on the surface as gilgai microtopography, with relief exceeding commonly 15 cm (Fig. 10.35)."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "107cf3dc-1829-42f8-b85c-ae2e26364833",
                                "sense_id": "de4ad0e1-34de-3a25-9f1f-0a74bde425a4",
                                "text": "One of its most remarkable features is its patterns of gilgai. The gilgais are small, almost circular depressions from a few centimetres to as much as 50 cm deep in the plain and several metres across."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
